# Every text file is LF in the index and in every checkout, on Windows too: oxfmt, the tracker check and the
# generated-file checks compare bytes. Git detects binaries; the extensions below are listed so detection never decides.
# SDP fixtures and Windows batch files keep the CRLF they were committed with.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sdp -text
*.bat -text
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.flac binary
*.ivf binary
*.gz binary
*.jar binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tflite binary

# Generated files. `pnpm run regen` rebuilds them from their sources.
# The `generated` merge driver keeps the current side without conflict markers
# (installed by `pnpm run hooks:install`; clones without it fall back to a normal merge).
# A kept side can be stale after a rebase, so run `pnpm run regen` and let
# `pnpm run check:generated` confirm before pushing.
apps/api/docs/generated-canonical-openapi.js linguist-generated merge=generated
apps/api/internal/adapters/postgres/sqlc/** linguist-generated merge=generated
apps/api/internal/obs/** linguist-generated merge=generated
